cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus or this code, please cite the article below."
title: "YouTube Safe Kids — sentiment analysis: corpus and code"
abstract: >-
  Annotated corpus of 2,749 sentences in Brazilian Portuguese, transcribed from 251
  public children's YouTube videos and labeled into three polarity classes by four
  annotators; the code that trains and evaluates a BERTimbau classifier, converts the
  prediction into an interpretable safety score and re-ranks search results by that
  score; and the YouTube Safe Kids platform, a web application that applies the score
  to live searches.
type: dataset
